  "final_message": "Order responses now include a `total` field in major units, so `12.5` means $12.50. The 39 tests pass, and the dependency check reports no violations (it also says 1 known violation is ignored, which I didn't look into).\n\n- **Where it applies:** `src/api/responses.ts` builds every order response, so `total` appears in `POST /orders`, `GET /orders/{id}`, `POST /orders/{id}/cancel`, and each order in `GET /orders`.\n- **Compatibility:** `totalCents` is unchanged and `total` is only added. That keeps the `GET /orders/{id}` response backward compatible for web-storefront (ARCH-8).\n- **Events:** I left `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` alone, since the storefront reads the REST responses.\n- **Other currencies:** `total` is in major units of the order's own currency. A 1250 JPY order gives `1250`, not `12.5`, because JPY and KRW have no minor unit.\n- **Tests:** I updated the two assertions in `test/app.test.ts` that check the exact response shape, and the `POST /orders` check now expects `total: 12.5`.\n- **Docs:** The response shape in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` still lists only `totalCents`. I didn't edit it because `CLAUDE.md` is the project instructions file. Say so if you want `total` added to both.",
